</span>



    <span class="we-customer-review__separator">, </span>

    <time data-test-customer-review-date datetime="2024-07-23T16:44:59.000Z" aria-label="July 23, 2024" class="we-customer-review__date" >07/23/2024</time>
  </div>

    <h3 class="we-truncate we-truncate--single-line  we-customer-review__title" dir="ltr" id="we-customer-review-1453">
    Great Simple App, Great Developer, Some Limitations
</h3>



      <blockquote class="we-truncate we-truncate--multi-line we-truncate--interactive  we-customer-review__body" dir>
        

        <p dir="false" data-test-bidi>I really love how simple and easy this app is to use. The pricing is also extremely reasonable for $0.99 when most apps charge way more just for some basic functions. I think it would be great if we would were able to create our own account so we can sync progress across different devices. <br /><br />I have ADHD and this app really helps me stay motivated and manage my executive dysfunction because I have to gamify EVERYTHING just to do simple things. I like how we are able to select different days for when we want to track a habit, but I wish we could select different reminder times for different days as well under the same habit. Say you want to add a yoga habit for each day, but want reminders at 2:00pm on certain days and 3:00pm on other days for those with varying schedules.<br /><br /> I also think sub-habit/task would be an interesting game changer. Say you’re trying to incorporate an entire morning routine habit, you can just label the habit morning routine, and you can click it to open, add a sub-habit/task, like make bed, brush teeth, do skin care, and once you check off all three of those things, it will complete that habit for the day. I feel like this would help with lessening the amount of habits you have to make when one habit can incorporate many things you want to do!</p>
    


<!----></blockquote>



      <h3 class="we-customer-review__header we-customer-review__header--response">
          <span class="we-truncate we-truncate--single-line  we-customer-review__title" dir="ltr">
